WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:09.040
Okay, so now moving on to the final task that I usually do in order to monitor and manage the indexes

00:09.080 --> 00:16.400
is to monitor the index fragmentations over the time as your data is inserted, updated, deleted into

00:16.400 --> 00:17.200
your tables.

00:17.680 --> 00:20.280
Indexes can become fragmented.

00:20.280 --> 00:21.560
So what is fragmentation?

00:21.560 --> 00:28.120
It means like there is unused spaces in your databases and the database is not filling them, or your

00:28.120 --> 00:31.320
data is not anymore sorted correctly in the index.

00:31.320 --> 00:37.120
And this of course leads to inefficient use of their storage and as well can slow down your queries.

00:43.240 --> 00:48.000
And in SQL, in order to get everything organized again we have two methods.

00:48.040 --> 00:50.240
The first method is reorganize.

00:50.240 --> 00:56.360
So it's going to go and defragment the leaf level of the index in order to get it organized and sorted

00:56.360 --> 00:58.560
again with the logical order.

00:58.800 --> 01:03.750
So it is very light operation and it will not block the user from using your table.

01:03.750 --> 01:06.030
And the second method called rebuild.

01:06.070 --> 01:08.030
This is heavyweight operation.

01:08.030 --> 01:12.830
It's going to go and drop the whole index and recreate it from the scratch.

01:12.990 --> 01:18.510
And this means of course, not only the data going to get sorted again, but as well the fragmentations

01:18.510 --> 01:22.190
inside your data pages and the index can be eliminated.

01:22.390 --> 01:24.270
So let's see how we can do that in SQL.

01:24.310 --> 01:24.550
Okay.

01:24.590 --> 01:26.070
So now back to our database.

01:26.070 --> 01:31.230
And the first question that you have to ask do we have an issue with the fragmentations in our indexes.

01:31.310 --> 01:34.830
So we have to check the health of our indexes in the database.

01:34.990 --> 01:39.950
And in order to do that we have again to go to the system metadata that we have.

01:39.990 --> 01:43.390
And we're going to check their dynamic management functions.

01:43.430 --> 01:47.470
So there is like a special functions in order to get an answer in the SQL server.

01:47.510 --> 01:48.430
Let's go and do that.

01:48.430 --> 01:51.990
So we're going to go and select star from the function.

01:51.990 --> 01:53.710
So it is system dot.

01:53.750 --> 02:00.190
So it's going to be system.dm db index physical states.

02:00.190 --> 02:00.670
This one.

02:00.670 --> 02:03.100
And this is a function that we have to pass few parameters.

02:03.100 --> 02:04.220
We will not go in details.

02:04.220 --> 02:05.380
Just follow me with this.

02:05.380 --> 02:09.300
So we have to give it the db id and the null.

02:09.740 --> 02:12.260
Another null and a third null.

02:12.260 --> 02:14.500
And the last one I'm going to be limited.

02:14.500 --> 02:15.940
So we have to do it like this.

02:15.940 --> 02:17.420
So let's go and query it.

02:17.460 --> 02:18.260
Now what do we find.

02:18.260 --> 02:19.500
We have the object ID.

02:19.500 --> 02:22.300
We have the index ID and few other formations.

02:22.300 --> 02:26.900
But the most important one is the average fragmentation in percent.

02:26.900 --> 02:31.060
So this column gives us the degree of the fragmentation in our index.

02:31.060 --> 02:33.620
If it is zero, then it is perfect.

02:33.620 --> 02:38.180
We have no fragmentation in the index and our index is very healthy.

02:38.180 --> 02:44.540
But if it is like 100, then that means it is completely out of order and we have to do something about

02:44.540 --> 02:44.860
it.

02:44.860 --> 02:48.860
And now you might say, you know what, I don't know which object does and which index.

02:48.860 --> 02:54.620
Well, you have to go and join few tables like the system dot tables and six dot index in order to get

02:54.620 --> 02:55.740
those informations.

02:55.740 --> 02:59.500
So we have to go and do that like we have done the first query okay.

02:59.540 --> 03:00.820
So offline I have done that.

03:00.820 --> 03:06.570
So I joined with the tables and the their indexes, and I'm sorting the data by the average recommendations

03:06.570 --> 03:11.610
and percentage descending in order to get the problems at the start, because we are interested where

03:11.610 --> 03:12.930
we have high percentage.

03:12.930 --> 03:14.730
So let's go and execute this.

03:14.770 --> 03:18.970
And now since it is practicing database, I didn't insert any data and so on.

03:18.970 --> 03:22.050
But in real projects you will get here different numbers.

03:22.290 --> 03:25.130
And here is my recommendations about the percentage.

03:25.130 --> 03:30.490
If the fragmentation is between like zero and ten, that means everything is like okay and you don't

03:30.490 --> 03:31.890
have to do anything about it.

03:31.890 --> 03:37.730
But if the percentage is between like ten and 30, then here we have to do something about it.

03:37.730 --> 03:43.130
So here I recommend to use the reorganize methods in order to sort the data again correctly.

03:43.130 --> 03:49.810
But if you have more than 30%, then here my recommendation is to go and rebuild the whole index because

03:49.810 --> 03:55.730
not only the data is in wrong order, but as well there is unused spaces in your database in the index,

03:55.730 --> 03:57.210
so you have to do something about it.

03:57.210 --> 03:59.410
So now let's go and imagine one of those indexes.

03:59.410 --> 04:03.880
For example this one over here has fragmentation of 15%.

04:03.920 --> 04:07.000
So now what we have to do is to go and reorganize this index.

04:07.000 --> 04:08.320
Let's see how we can do that.

04:08.320 --> 04:12.600
So let's go over here and say the following alter index.

04:12.600 --> 04:14.480
And then we need the index name.

04:14.480 --> 04:16.520
So let's go and get it from here.

04:16.800 --> 04:19.800
And then you have to mention the table name where the index exists.

04:19.800 --> 04:21.440
So we have it from the customers.

04:21.440 --> 04:24.160
So from sales customers.

04:24.160 --> 04:25.720
So now we are editing the index.

04:25.720 --> 04:27.760
And we have to tell SQL what to do now.

04:27.760 --> 04:29.800
So we just want to reorganize the index.

04:29.800 --> 04:32.160
So you go and use the keyword reorganize.

04:32.160 --> 04:35.320
So reorganize and that's it.

04:35.320 --> 04:36.360
This is very simple.

04:36.360 --> 04:38.840
So let's go and do that and let's go and see.

04:38.840 --> 04:39.680
It is completed.

04:39.680 --> 04:42.000
And it was very fast because we have small database.

04:42.000 --> 04:45.800
But sometimes it takes a little more time if you have a big index and big table.

04:45.800 --> 04:51.080
So after reorganizing you can go and again check the table over here and see the results.

04:51.080 --> 04:52.960
And it should be like here zero.

04:53.000 --> 04:57.880
Now let's see that we have another index where the fragmentation around like 50%.

04:57.920 --> 04:59.680
So let's go and copy it.

04:59.680 --> 05:03.880
And this time instead of reorganize we're going to do rebuild.

05:03.880 --> 05:05.830
So I'm going to take the whole thing.

05:06.590 --> 05:11.350
And this time we're going to go and rebuild this index over here on the same table.

05:11.350 --> 05:14.110
And instead of reorganize we're going to say rebuild.

05:14.510 --> 05:17.110
So let's go and execute that.

05:17.110 --> 05:21.750
And with that SQL did drop the whole index and created from the scratch.

05:21.750 --> 05:25.470
And this is usually takes more time than reorganize of course.

05:25.510 --> 05:29.630
And the next step of course is to go and check again the fragmentations and so on.

05:29.630 --> 05:36.350
So that's all about how to make your index healthy and remove the fragmentations from your index.

05:36.870 --> 05:37.790
All right my friends.

05:37.790 --> 05:42.710
So as you can see, improving the performance of your queries doesn't end by creating them.

05:42.710 --> 05:44.990
It's all about staying proactive.

05:45.190 --> 05:51.150
So monitor the usage of the indexes, check whether there are any missing indexes, and always make

05:51.190 --> 05:54.190
sure that statistics of the database are up to date.

05:54.190 --> 05:58.950
And keep your eyes on the fragmentations and make sure you have healthy indexes.

05:58.950 --> 06:04.150
So with that, you have learned how I manage and monitor the indexes once I create them, and I really

06:04.150 --> 06:05.910
recommend you to follow those steps.
